// Title: New BgInfo.EXE Custom DB Path Registry Configuration
// Sigma ID: 53330955-dc52-487f-a3a2-da24dcff99b5
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects setting of a new registry database value related to BgInfo configuration. Attackers can
//   for example set this value to save the results of the commands executed by BgInfo in order to
//   exfiltrate information.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of external DB to save the results
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_bginfo_custom_db.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Software\\Winternals\\BGInfo\\Database"
